      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "5 . In a unit cube, there are 3 types of triangles, with side lengths \\((1,1, \\sqrt{2}),(1, \\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{3})\\) and \\((\\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{2})\\). Together they generate 5 different angle values.",
